# Systematic-GROUP importance scan against a single cache.
#
#   scripts/submit_fanout.sh --queue capacity --walltime 03:00:00 \
#       --variants jobs/contours/scan_systgroup.variants \
#       jobs/contours/contours_full.ini -- surface -g 30 --xlo 1e-2 --ylo 1e-1
#
# Companion to scan_detsyst.variants, which scans individual detector
# systematics. This one removes whole groups: flux, the interaction model (as a
# block and broken down), POT normalization, and G4 reinteractions.
#
# 16 variants = 16 nodes, exactly capacity's ceiling. Comment lines out
# to shrink the batch.
#
# EXCLUDING BY TAG. --exclude-systs resolves a tag before a name, so naming a
# tag drops every systematic carrying it - which is exactly what is wanted here.
# The counts below are the entries each tag covers in contours_base.xml.
#
# TAGS WITH SPACES CANNOT BE USED. The exclude field is whitespace-separated, so
# `POT Normalization` would arrive as two arguments, each matching nothing, each
# silently excluding nothing. The POT and detector lines therefore enumerate
# their member names instead. The same applies to `Cosmic Background
# Normalization` (its plotname `CORSIKA` is space-free and works if you want it)
# and `stat,MC Stats`.
#
# VERIFYING THESE IS NOT THE SAME AS FOR scan_detsyst.variants. Only spline,
# norm and hist1d systematics become fitted parameters; covariance systematics
# are marginalised analytically and never appear in global_fit.txt. So:
#
#   fitted   Cross-Section-QE/MEC/RES/DIS/COH/NCEL/FSI (spline), POT and
#            detector systematics (hist1d)
#            -> parameter count in global_fit.txt drops, as with the detsyst scan
#   NOT      Flux, G4, Cross-Section-NonRES-nu/nubar, mcstat (covariance)
#   fitted   -> parameter count is UNCHANGED even when the exclusion worked.
#               Confirm those from the fractional systematics breakdown or the
#               contour instead, not the parameter list.
#
# label            exclude
# --- the three coarse groups ---
noflux             Flux
nointeraction      Cross-Section-QE Cross-Section-MEC Cross-Section-RES Cross-Section-NonRES-nu Cross-Section-NonRES-nubar Cross-Section-DIS Cross-Section-COH Cross-Section-NCEL Cross-Section-FSI
nopot              ToroidCalibration_sbnd_Run1 ToroidCalibration_icarus_Run2 ToroidCalibration_icarus_Run4 ProtonMiss_sbnd_Run1 ProtonMiss_icarus_Run2 ProtonMiss_icarus_Run4
# --- G4 reinteractions ---
nog4               G4
# --- all detector systematics at once (scan_detsyst.variants does them singly) ---
nodetsys           ChargeScale15_sbnd_Run1 ChargeScale_icarus_Run2 ChargeScale_icarus_Run4 SCE_icarus_Run2 SCE_icarus_Run4 TriggerEmulation_sbnd_Run1 TriggerEmulation_icarus_Run2 TriggerEmulation_icarus_Run4 WireModxThetaXW_sbnd_Run1 WireModxThetaXW_icarus_Run2 WireModxThetaXW_icarus_Run4 WireModYZ_sbnd_Run1 WireModYZ_icarus_Run2 WireModYZ_icarus_Run4 DENT_sbnd_Run1
# --- cosmic background normalization ---
# Its tag ("Cosmic Background Normalization") has spaces, but unlike the POT and
# detector groups this is a single entry whose PLOTNAME is space-free, and
# --exclude-systs falls back to the plotname map. It is a 30% norm on the SBND
# out-of-time cosmics only (pattern .*SBND_.*cos), so expect a small effect.
nocorsika          CORSIKA
# --- MC statistical uncertainty ---
# Addressed by its XML text content, not its tag or plotname: the tag is
# "stat,MC Stats" (comma-joined, second half has a space) and the plotname
# "MC Stats" has a space. `mcstat` is the key its covariance is registered
# under - see PROconfig.h m_mcstat_systname and PROsyst.cxx syst_map. Removing
# it shows how much of the contour width is finite MC statistics rather than
# systematics. It is a Covariance, so the parameter count will NOT change.
nomcstat           mcstat
# --- interaction model, broken down (subsets of nointeraction above) ---
noqe               Cross-Section-QE
nomec              Cross-Section-MEC
nores              Cross-Section-RES
nononresnu         Cross-Section-NonRES-nu
nononresnubar      Cross-Section-NonRES-nubar
nodis              Cross-Section-DIS
nocoh              Cross-Section-COH
noncel             Cross-Section-NCEL
nofsi              Cross-Section-FSI
